1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
A complete first mission, captured from the game. Scripted controller inputs; live physics and survival.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:12,000
No space knowledge is needed. Follow the cyan SCAN marker and the objective at the upper left.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Read the dashboard: AIR is breathing oxygen. TOOL BATTERY powers scans. SUIT is integrity.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:33,000
WASD moves and the mouse looks. The destination distance decreases as you approach.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:43,100
Air and battery fall outside shelter. In this first mission, construction is optional.

6
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:46,130
Hold E near the target for three seconds. A completed scan consumes 8 battery.

7
00:00:46,130 --> 00:00:51,130
The light scanner records a rock observation. A clue supports investigation; it is not proof of life.

8
00:00:51,130 --> 00:00:55,130
The learning screen explains the interpretation, then points you toward the next observation.

9
00:00:55,130 --> 00:01:10,000
The second target uses a drill. Different instruments reveal different kinds of evidence.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:24,000
NASA MOLA supplies regional elevation context. Local rocks, routes and discoveries are game scenarios.

11
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:37,200
Watch the remaining air and tool battery while you travel. Return to shelter if reserves are low.

12
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:40,230
Hold E again. Two distinct observations are required before the first return.

13
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:45,230
This time the scripted player tries the overclaim. The game explains why it is not supported.

14
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:49,230
A mistaken scientific explanation is a learning moment in practice, not a campaign penalty.

15
00:01:49,230 --> 00:02:04,000
With both observations collected, follow HOME back to the white crew shelter.

16
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:19,000
The shelter restores breathing air and battery during active field play. Menus pause the simulation.

17
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:33,260
Approach the main habitat and press E. The return action unlocks when you have both observations.

18
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:38,260
Choose RETURN TO EARTH. Practice progress is separate from campaign funds and checkpoints.

19
00:02:38,260 --> 00:02:43,260
Ascent is committed. The rendered spacecraft and camera show the crew leaving the surface.

20
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:49,300
Debrief: two observations and a safe return. Continue into the Earth lab to design your own campaign.
